# The help editor (hedit.c, lookup.c's help_lookup and had_lookup), with Planner (security 9) and Delver (security
# 0), and the fixture area olcsave.are (tools/fixtures/files), which has a help of its own. The string editor's
# "@" is sent as "x", a backspace, "@" (see redit.scn).
# - hedit with nothing, and a help that isn't; "hedit new" with no name opens a help named "new" rather than
#   giving new's syntax; "edit help" isn't the help editor (edit's word for it is "hedit"), though new's syntax
#   says so
# - edit QMCONFIG (help.are): show, commands, ?, an unknown word, keyword, level and its refusals, text in the
#   string editor, list (all, and this area's, which has none), new (exists; in help.are by its file name)
# - a new help in Midgaard, which has none: a help file for it, and the area marked changed
# - in the fixture area: changing its help marks the help file changed but not the area, so asave changed saves
#   no zone and then writes the help file, which is the area's own file: olcsave.are is left with only its helps
# - delete: of a help someone else is editing too (it takes them out of the editor), of a file's first help, and of
#   its last: a help made after that is never in the file's list, nor in the list of all helps (help_last is
#   left on the deleted one too), so hedit can't find it, and the editor puts its builder out at the next line
# - Delver can open a help, and is put out at his next line; the prompt's %o and %O
@place olcsave.are olcsave.are
@place area-olcsave.lst area.lst
@connect b
Planner
smoke123
@return
@return
scroll 0
goto 3001
hedit
hedit nonsuch
hedit new
edit help qmconfig
edit hedit qmconfig
@return
show
commands
?
xyzzy
keyword
keyword QMCONFIG QM
level
level x
level 99
level 5
text
.s
One more line.
x@
show
text x
list
list all
list area
new
new qmconfig
new help.are TESTHELP
show
level 1
done
hedit new MIDHELP
level 3
done
goto 30200
hedit olcsave
level 2
done
asave changed
@file olcsave.are
@file help.are
hedit new AAA
done
hedit new BBB
done
@connect d
Delver
psswrd
@return
hedit bbb
@as b
hedit bbb
delete
@as d
show
hedit qmconfig
show
@as b
hedit aaa
list area
done
hedit new CCC
list area
done
hedit fresh
hedit new FRESH
done
hedit fresh
delete
hedit olcsave
delete
hedit new DDD
list area
list all
done
prompt <%o %O>
hedit qmconfig
done
prompt <%hhp %mm %vmv>
asave world
@file olcsave.are
